  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line 2 oven trays with baking paper. Peel the sweet potatoes, then cut into 1.5cm-wedges. Quarter the tomatoes. Finely chop the coriander, including the stems. Drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446853/photos/large/prep_ingredients-7f5f4a234e61a8ea6b243b152e8c4543.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast sweet potato: Put the sweet potato on a lined tray, drizzle with 1 tbs olive oil, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat. Roast on the upper oven shelf, turning halfway, for 15-20 mins until golden and tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446854/photos/large/roast_sweet_potato-2320bc978ee03971fce2431df1f783d9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast harissa chickpeas: Meanwhile, put the chickpeas, 2 tsp harissa seasoning (see Make it yours), 2 tsp olive oil and 2 tsp tomato paste in a bowl. Season with salt and stir to coat. Spread the chickpea mixture over the remaining lined tray and roast on the lower shelf for 10 mins or until crisp.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446855/photos/large/roast_harissa_chickpeas-3b78f0989f07d5a0181e1f4245eda143.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make tomato salsa: While the chickpeas are roasting, put the tomatoes, coriander, 2 tsp red wine vinegar, 2 tsp olive oil, 1 tsp dijon mustard and ¼ tsp sugar in a bowl. Season with salt and pepper and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446856/photos/large/make_tomato_salsa-246222c9c8b5928a4d6f693a2cff5826.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the sweet potato among plates and top with the harissa chickpeas and tomato salsa. Crumble over the feta and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446857/photos/large/serve_up-494b48a9ecf2b3cd8c7fa7ffd30ef16c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Harissa contains chilli, so if you're cooking for young children, add 1 tsp harissa seasoning to half the chickpea mixture and roast on separate ends of the oven tray.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446858/photos/large/kitchen_notes-648d7c160824c5f136874573b4a1cdf3.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
